<title>CANADA: Canadian Gas Association storage survey - April 25.</title>
<headline>Canadian Gas Association storage survey - April 25.</headline>
<dateline>CALGARY 1997-05-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>Canadian Gas Association (CGA) weekly survey of Canadian natural gas in storage in billion cubic feet (bcf):</p>
<p>							 Pct Full  Pct Full</p>
<p>		 04/25/97  04/18/97  Pct Full  Week Ago  Year Ago</p>
<p>East	     11.43	8.82     4.92	 3.79	3.8</p>
<p>West	     48.96     47.87    18.90	18.47     31.8</p>
<p>Total Canada   60.39     56.69    12.28	11.53     19.0</p>
<p>East-West division is the Manitoba/Saskatchewan and North Dakota/Minnesota borders.</p>
<p>East capacity 04/25/97: 232.55 bcf, 04/18/97: 232.55 bcf.  </p>
<p>West capacity 04/25/97: 259.11 bcf, 04/18/97: 259.11 bcf.</p>
<p>The Canadian Gas Association survey includes liquefied petroleum gas, all Canadian operators of gas storage and Canadian companies contracting gas storage in the U.S.</p>
<p>((--Calgary Bureau (403) 531-1624))</p>
</text>
